### Food Delivery Platform - Restaurant Service
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (named requests pass ids between calls).
### Run the requests from top to bottom. Needs user-service + restaurant-service (+ gateway).
###
### The caller is identified by the access token of a sign-in below (Authorization: Bearer); its role must be
###   RESTAURANT_ADMIN for /restaurants/mine/**, PLATFORM_ADMIN for /admin/**

# Everything through the API Gateway:
@gateway = http://localhost:8080
# The services' shared secret of the internal APIs: the dev profile's value (INTERNAL_SERVICE_TOKEN elsewhere)
@internalServiceToken = dev-internal-service-token
# Or call restaurant-service directly (user-service calls still need the gateway or port 8081):
# @gateway = http://localhost:8082

@adminEmail = admin@fooddelivery.local
@adminPassword = ChangeMe123

# Change before step 1 if this owner already exists (409 Conflict)
@ownerEmail = arjun.spicehub@example.com
@ownerPassword = Owner1234

# Every call carries the access token of a sign-in above (valid 15 minutes: sign in again after that).
@ownerToken = {{ownerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@restaurantId = {{submitRestaurant.response.body.$.id}}
@version = {{myRestaurant.response.body.$.version}}


### ======================== OWNER ACCOUNT (user-service) ========================

### 1. Register as a restaurant owner
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{ownerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{ownerPassword}}",
  "fullName": "Arjun Mehta",
  "phone": "+919811112222",
  "role": "RESTAURANT_ADMIN"
}

### 2. Log in as the owner -> ownerToken
# @name ownerLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{ownerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{ownerPassword}}"
}


### ============================ OWNER: ONBOARDING ============================

### 3. Submit a restaurant (201, status PENDING) -> restaurantId
# @name submitRestaurant
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Spice Hub",
  "description": "Hyderabadi biryani and kebabs",
  "cuisines": ["Biryani", "North Indian"],
  "phone": "+919876543210",
  "email": "contact@spicehub.example.com",
  "address": {
    "line1": "45 Brigade Road",
    "city": "Bengaluru",
    "state": "Karnataka",
    "postalCode": "560025",
    "country": "India",
    "latitude": 12.971600,
    "longitude": 77.607300
  },
  "timeZone": "Asia/Kolkata",
  "legalBusinessName": "Spice Hub Foods Pvt Ltd",
  "taxRegistrationNumber": "29ABCDE1234F1Z5",
  "foodLicenseNumber": "11223344556677",
  "documents": [
    { "type": "FOOD_LICENSE", "url": "https://docs.example.com/spice-hub/fssai.pdf" },
    { "type": "TAX_REGISTRATION", "url": "https://docs.example.com/spice-hub/gst.pdf" }
  ],
  "operatingHours": [
    { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY",    "opensAt": "11:00", "closesAt": "15:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY",    "opensAt": "18:00", "closesAt": "23:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "TUESDAY",   "opensAt": "11:00", "closesAt": "23:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "WEDNESDAY", "opensAt": "11:00", "closesAt": "23:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "THURSDAY",  "opensAt": "11:00", "closesAt": "23:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "FRIDAY",    "opensAt": "11:00", "closesAt": "23:30" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "SATURDAY",  "opensAt": "10:00", "closesAt": "23:30" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "SUNDAY",    "opensAt": "10:00", "closesAt": "23:00" }
  ]
}

### 4. Business rule example: overlapping hours (422)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Overlap Cafe",
  "cuisines": ["Cafe"],
  "phone": "+919876543211",
  "email": "hello@overlap.example.com",
  "address": { "line1": "1 Test Street", "city": "Bengaluru", "state": "Karnataka", "postalCode": "560001", "country": "India" },
  "legalBusinessName": "Overlap Cafe LLP",
  "foodLicenseNumber": "99887766554433",
  "documents": [ { "type": "FOOD_LICENSE", "url": "https://docs.example.com/overlap/fssai.pdf" } ],
  "operatingHours": [
    { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY", "opensAt": "09:00", "closesAt": "14:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY", "opensAt": "13:00", "closesAt": "18:00" }
  ]
}

### 5. List my restaurants (all statuses)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 6. My restaurant: status, review reason and current version -> version
# @name myRestaurant
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 7. Not visible to customers while PENDING (404)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}


### =========================== ADMIN: REVIEW ===========================

### 8. Log in as the platform admin -> adminToken
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 9. Pending approvals, oldest first
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/restaurants?status=PENDING&sort=createdAt,asc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 10. Review details: business info, documents, hours + owner (fetched from user-service)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 11. Reject with a reason the owner will see
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Food license document is unreadable. Please upload a clearer scan."
}


### ===================== OWNER: FIX AND RESUBMIT =====================

### 12. Owner reads the rejection reason (run step 6 again to refresh the version)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 13. Owner uploads a new document link. Run step 6 first so {{version}} is current.
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": {{version}},
  "name": "Spice Hub",
  "description": "Hyderabadi biryani and kebabs",
  "cuisines": ["Biryani", "North Indian"],
  "phone": "+919876543210",
  "email": "contact@spicehub.example.com",
  "address": { "line1": "45 Brigade Road", "city": "Bengaluru", "state": "Karnataka", "postalCode": "560025", "country": "India" },
  "timeZone": "Asia/Kolkata",
  "legalBusinessName": "Spice Hub Foods Pvt Ltd",
  "taxRegistrationNumber": "29ABCDE1234F1Z5",
  "foodLicenseNumber": "11223344556677",
  "documents": [
    { "type": "FOOD_LICENSE", "url": "https://docs.example.com/spice-hub/fssai-clear-scan.pdf" },
    { "type": "TAX_REGISTRATION", "url": "https://docs.example.com/spice-hub/gst.pdf" }
  ],
  "operatingHours": [
    { "dayOfWeek": "MONDAY",    "opensAt": "11:00", "closesAt": "23:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "TUESDAY",   "opensAt": "11:00", "closesAt": "23:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "WEDNESDAY", "opensAt": "11:00", "closesAt": "23:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "THURSDAY",  "opensAt": "11:00", "closesAt": "23:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "FRIDAY",    "opensAt": "11:00", "closesAt": "23:30" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "SATURDAY",  "opensAt": "10:00", "closesAt": "23:30" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "SUNDAY",    "opensAt": "10:00", "closesAt": "23:00" }
  ]
}

### 14. Send it for review again (REJECTED -> PENDING)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/resubmit
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}


### ======================= ADMIN: APPROVE AND GO LIVE =======================

### 15. Approve (PENDING -> APPROVED)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "License and tax documents verified"
}

### 16. Activate (APPROVED -> ACTIVE): customers can now see it
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Menu and payout details ready"
}


### ============================ CUSTOMERS ============================

### 17. Browse active restaurants in a city, by cuisine
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants?city=Bengaluru&cuisine=biryani&page=0&size=20&sort=name,asc

### 18. Restaurant page: hours and whether it is open now (no business data)
###     Cached in Redis (Phase 12) until the restaurant changes; "openNow" is worked out on every request.
###     See the cached copy: docker exec -it fd-redis redis-cli --scan --pattern "restaurant:v1:details:*"
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}


### ======================= OWNER: OPENING HOURS =======================

### 19-20. Run step 6 again first (refreshes {{version}}), then replace the weekly schedule (closed on Mondays now)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/operating-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": {{version}},
  "operatingHours": [
    { "dayOfWeek": "TUESDAY",   "opensAt": "11:00", "closesAt": "23:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "WEDNESDAY", "opensAt": "11:00", "closesAt": "23:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "THURSDAY",  "opensAt": "11:00", "closesAt": "23:00" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "FRIDAY",    "opensAt": "11:00", "closesAt": "23:30" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "SATURDAY",  "opensAt": "10:00", "closesAt": "23:30" },
    { "dayOfWeek": "SUNDAY",    "opensAt": "10:00", "closesAt": "23:00" }
  ]
}

### 21. Same request again with the old version: 409 (optimistic locking)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/operating-hours
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": {{version}},
  "operatingHours": [
    { "dayOfWeek": "SUNDAY", "opensAt": "10:00", "closesAt": "22:00" }
  ]
}


### ======================== ADMIN: CONTROL ========================

### 22. Suspend (policy violation): hidden from customers
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/suspend
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Repeated hygiene complaints - under investigation"
}

### 23. Reinstate (SUSPENDED -> ACTIVE)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Inspection passed"
}

### 24. Invalid transition example: approve an ACTIVE restaurant (409)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Testing the state machine"
}

### 25. Audit history (newest first)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 26. Identity headers without a token name nobody (the gateway removes them): 401
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine
X-User-Id: 999
X-User-Role: RESTAURANT_ADMIN


### ======================= EVENTS (Kafka, Phases 7-8) =======================
### Every change writes RestaurantChanged (topic fooddelivery.restaurant.changed, key = restaurantId) to the
### transactional outbox: SUBMITTED, PROFILE_UPDATED (details or opening hours) and STATUS_CHANGED (admin
### decisions, resubmit). Each event carries the restaurant's new version; catalog-service keeps a copy.
### Messages: Kafka UI http://localhost:8090

### RestaurantChanged schema in Schema Registry
GET http://localhost:8091/subjects/fooddelivery.restaurant.changed-value/versions/latest

### Internal API (other services, not routed by the gateway): now includes the version
GET http://localhost:8082/api/v1/internal/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}
X-Service-Token: {{internalServiceToken}}

### Since Phase 11 the event also carries description and cuisines (for search). To fill or rebuild the search
### index with every restaurant already in MySQL, replay the current state as REPUBLISHED events
### (audited, changes no data; consumers ignore versions they already have):
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/restaurants/events/republish
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### ========================= OPERATIONS =========================

### Health (direct)
GET http://localhost:8082/actuator/health

### Swagger UI: http://localhost:8082/swagger-ui.html
GET http://localhost:8082/v3/api-docs
